< \r\ntcc gets (a POSIX program):
^ \r\n  in, out, err         the terminal
^ \r\n  ~/project            read (current directory)
^ \r\n  ~/project/main.c     read (operand FILE)
^ \r\n  ~/project            create and change anything in (option -o)
^ \r\n  ~/include            read (+r)
^ \r\n  /bin /usr /etc       read (system)
^ \r\n  /proc/self/exe       read (system)
^ \r\n  /tmp                 change anything in (this line's own)
^ \r\n  /dev/null
